module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeryAmpleTwist.CanonicalSymHom
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.EventualSurjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.DegreeOneProducts
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Projective.Basic

/-!
# Stacks Tag 0B3U: the relative `Proj` of an algebra generated in degree one is projective

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝒜` a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra generated by `𝒜_1` over `𝒜_0`
with `𝒜_1` of finite type. Stacks Tag 0B3U says that `Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ S` is projective, and its
one-line proof is that the canonical graded-algebra map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` induces a closed immersion
`Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)`.

Both halves are now available: the canonical map is
`Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymHom` and the closed immersion is Stacks Tag 07ZK (2).
What this file supplies is the input Tag 07ZK asks of the map — that it be surjective on
homogeneous sections over the affine opens of the base in all large degrees — and then reads the
closed immersion as projectivity.

## Why the canonical map is surjective in positive degrees

Over an affine open `U` of the base, generation in degree one says that the graded ring of
sections is generated by its degree-one part over its degree-zero part, and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.eq_top_of_mul_mem_of_adjoin_eq_top`
reads that back on the homogeneous pieces: the degree-`d + 1` sections are additively generated by
the products of a degree-`d` section with a degree-one one. The image of the canonical map in each
degree is an additive subgroup of the sections, it contains the degree-one sections because the
map is the identity there, and it is closed under those products because the map is multiplicative
— so an induction on the degree makes it everything in every degree `≥ 1`. In degree zero the map
is the unit `𝒪_S ⟶ 𝒜_0` and need not be surjective, which is why the hypothesis the source's
citation carries is "in all sufficiently large degrees".

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple.projHom`: the morphism `Proj_S(B) ⟶ Proj_S(A)` attached by Stacks Tag
  07ZG to a homomorphism of graded algebras whose domain of definition is everything.
* `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom`: the morphism `Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)` of
  Stacks Tag 07ZR, attached to the canonical map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.eventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections_canonicalSymHom`: **the
  canonical map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` is surjective on homogeneous sections over every affine open of the
  base in every positive degree.**
* `Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.isClosedImmersion_canonicalSymProjHom` and
  `canonicalSymProjHom_comp_toBase`: **the closed immersion `Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)` over `S`**,
  the closed-immersion clause of Stacks Tag 07ZR.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isProjective_relativeProj_toBase`: **Stacks Tag 0B3U.**

## Implementation notes

**The chain of Tag 07ZK is restated over the surjectivity hypothesis.** Everything in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.EventualSurjective` downstream of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.eventually_surjective_gradedAddHom` uses the
hypothesis `∀ᶠ d, Epi (ψ.app d)` only through
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.EventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections`, which that
file derives from it. The four declarations in the first section below are those statements over
the weaker hypothesis, which is the one available here: this repository has the implication from
an epimorphism of quasi-coherent modules to surjectivity on the sections over an affine open
(`Stacks.SectionEpiAffine.surjective_app_of_isAffineOpen`) and not its converse.

**The degree-one factor is on the right throughout.** A product of a degree-`d` and a degree-one
section lands in `Γ(𝒜_{(d : ℤ) + 1}, U)`, which is the degree-`d + 1` summand of the section ring
on the nose; written the other way round it would land in degree `1 + (d : ℤ)` and every statement
would carry a transport.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B3U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B3U)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07ZK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07ZK)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01W8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01W8)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite Filter
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain
open Stacks.SymGraded

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {A B : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S} (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B)

/-- Over an affine open of the base the induced homomorphism of graded rings of sections is
surjective on homogeneous components of all sufficiently large degree. This is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain.eventually_surjective_gradedAddHom` over the
surjectivity hypothesis rather than over epimorphy. -/
public theorem eventually_surjective_gradedAddHom_of_affineSections
    (hψ : EventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections ψ) {V : S.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    ∀ᶠ d : ℕ in atTop,
      Function.Surjective (GradedRingHom.gradedAddHom (ψ.sectionHom V) d) :=
  (hψ V hV).mono fun _ hd => surjective_gradedAddHom_of_surjective_sectionPieceHom ψ hd

/-- Over an affine open of the base the induced morphism of projective spectra is defined
everywhere. -/
public theorem chartDomain_eq_top_of_affineSections
    (hψ : EventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections ψ) {V : S.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) :
    ψ.chartDomain V = ⊤ :=
  RelativeProjChain.mapDomain_eq_top_of_eventually_surjective (A.grading V) (B.grading V)
    (ψ.sectionHom V) (eventually_surjective_gradedAddHom_of_affineSections ψ hψ hV)

/-- **Stacks 07ZI (1) and 07ZK (1)** over the surjectivity hypothesis: the domain of definition of
`ψ` is all of `Proj_S(B)`. -/
public theorem relativeMapDomain_eq_top_of_affineSections
    (hψ : EventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections ψ) : ψ.relativeMapDomain = ⊤ :=
  (ψ.relativeMapDomain_unique ⊤ fun _ hV =>
    (chartDomain_eq_top_of_affineSections ψ hψ hV).symm).symm

/-- **Stacks 07ZI (2) and 07ZK (2)** over the surjectivity hypothesis: the morphism `r_ψ` of
Stacks Tag 07ZG is a closed immersion. -/
public theorem isClosedImmersion_relativeMapHom_of_affineSections
    (hψ : EventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections ψ) :
    IsClosedImmersion (Tag07ZGMorphism.relativeMapHom ψ) :=
  Tag07ZGMorphism.of_forall_chart ψ (P := @IsClosedImmersion) fun V =>
    RelativeProjChain.isClosedImmersion_mapHom_of_eventually_surjective (A.grading V.1)
      (B.grading V.1) (ψ.sectionHom V.1)
      (eventually_surjective_gradedAddHom_of_affineSections ψ hψ V.2)

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjMapDomain

/-! ### Tag 07ZG's morphism when its domain of definition is everything -/

namespace Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} {A B : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S} (ψ : SheafGradedAlgebraHom A B)

/-- **The identification of `Proj_S(B)` with the domain of definition of `ψ`**, when the latter is
everything. -/
def topDomainIso (hdom : ψ.relativeMapDomain = ⊤) :
    (relativeProj B).scheme ≅ ψ.relativeMapDomain.toScheme :=
  (relativeProj B).scheme.topIso.symm ≪≫ (relativeProj B).scheme.isoOfEq hdom.symm

/-- The identification of `Proj_S(B)` with the domain of definition of `ψ`, followed by the
inclusion of that domain, is the identity. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem topDomainIso_hom_ι (hdom : ψ.relativeMapDomain = ⊤) :
    (topDomainIso ψ hdom).hom ≫ ψ.relativeMapDomain.ι = 𝟙 _ := by
  rw [topDomainIso, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, Category.assoc, Scheme.isoOfEq_hom_ι,
    Scheme.toIso_inv_ι]

/-- **The morphism `Proj_S(B) ⟶ Proj_S(A)` attached to `ψ`** when its domain of definition is the
whole of `Proj_S(B)`: the morphism `r_ψ` of Stacks Tag 07ZG, read through that identification. -/
def projHom (hdom : ψ.relativeMapDomain = ⊤) :
    (relativeProj B).scheme ⟶ (relativeProj A).scheme :=
  (topDomainIso ψ hdom).hom ≫ Tag07ZGMorphism.relativeMapHom ψ

/-- **The morphism is a morphism over the base.** Tag 07ZG's morphism is one over the inclusion of
its domain of definition, and that inclusion cancels the identification of the previous
definition. -/
theorem projHom_comp_toBase (hdom : ψ.relativeMapDomain = ⊤) :
    projHom ψ hdom ≫ (relativeProj A).toBase = (relativeProj B).toBase := by
  rw [projHom, Category.assoc, Tag07ZGMorphism.relativeMapHom_comp_toBase,
    topDomainIso_hom_ι_assoc]

/-- The morphism `projHom` is a closed immersion as soon as Tag 07ZG's morphism is. -/
private theorem isClosedImmersion_projHom_of (hdom : ψ.relativeMapDomain = ⊤)
    (h : IsClosedImmersion (Tag07ZGMorphism.relativeMapHom ψ)) :
    IsClosedImmersion (projHom ψ hdom) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsClosedImmersion ((topDomainIso ψ hdom).hom ≫ _))

/-- **The morphism is a closed immersion** as soon as `ψ` is an epimorphism in all sufficiently
large degrees: this is Stacks Tag 07ZK (2) composed with an isomorphism of schemes. -/
theorem isClosedImmersion_projHom (hψ : ∀ᶠ d : ℕ in atTop, Epi (ψ.app (d : ℤ))) :
    IsClosedImmersion (projHom ψ (relativeMapDomain_eq_top_of_eventually_epi ψ hψ)) :=
  isClosedImmersion_projHom_of ψ _ (isClosedImmersion_relativeMapHom_of_eventually_epi ψ hψ)

end Stacks.Tag07ZRVeryAmple

namespace Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S)

/-! ### The canonical map is the identity on degree-one sections -/

/-- The canonical map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` carries the degree-one generator of a local section of
`𝒜_1` back to that section. -/
theorem canonicalSymHom_app_one_apply (U : S.Opens) (a : Γ(A.piece 1, U)) :
    ((canonicalSymHom A).app 1).app U
      (Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1)) U a) = a := by
  have h := congrArg (fun f : A.piece 1 ⟶ A.piece 1 => (Scheme.Modules.Hom.app f U) a)
    (symmetricAlgebraGen_comp_canonicalSymHom_app_one A)
  simp only [Scheme.Modules.Hom.id_app, CategoryTheory.id_apply] at h
  exact h

/-! ### Surjectivity in positive degrees -/

/-- **The canonical map is surjective on degree-one sections over every open**, being the identity
there. -/
theorem range_canonicalSymHom_sectionPieceHom_one (U : S.Opens) :
    ((canonicalSymHom A).sectionPieceHom U 1).range = ⊤ :=
  top_unique fun a _ =>
    ⟨Scheme.Modules.Hom.app (Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraGen S (A.piece 1)) U a,
      canonicalSymHom_app_one_apply A U a⟩

/-- **The canonical map is surjective on homogeneous sections of every positive degree over an
affine open of the base**, as soon as `𝒜` is generated by `𝒜_1` over `𝒜_0`.

The induction is on the degree. In degree one the map is the identity. In the step the image is an
additive subgroup of the degree-`d + 2` sections which, `ψ` being multiplicative, contains every
product of a degree-`d + 1` section with a degree-one one, both factors being in the image
already; generation in degree one makes such a subgroup everything. -/
theorem range_canonicalSymHom_sectionPieceHom_succ
    (hgen : ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A) {U : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) :
    ∀ d : ℕ, ((canonicalSymHom A).sectionPieceHom U (d + 1)).range = ⊤ := by
  intro d
  induction d with
  | zero => exact range_canonicalSymHom_sectionPieceHom_one A U
  | succ d ih =>
      refine SheafGradedAlgebra.eq_top_of_mul_mem_of_adjoin_eq_top A U (hgen U hU) (d + 1) _ ?_
      intro y x
      obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ : y ∈ ((canonicalSymHom A).sectionPieceHom U (d + 1)).range := by
        rw [ih]; trivial
      obtain ⟨w, rfl⟩ : x ∈ ((canonicalSymHom A).sectionPieceHom U 1).range := by
        rw [range_canonicalSymHom_sectionPieceHom_one]; trivial
      exact ⟨((symAlgebra (A.piece 1)).mul ((d + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) 1).app U v w,
        (canonicalSymHom A).app_mul ((d + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) 1 U v w⟩

/-- **The canonical map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` is surjective on homogeneous sections over every affine
open of the base in all sufficiently large degrees**, which is the hypothesis Stacks Tags 07ZI and
07ZK ask of a homomorphism of graded algebras. Every degree `≥ 1` works. -/
theorem eventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections_canonicalSymHom
    (hgen : ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A) :
    EventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections (canonicalSymHom A) := by
  intro U hU
  refine eventually_atTop.2 ⟨1, fun d hd b => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨e, rfl⟩ : ∃ e : ℕ, d = e + 1 := ⟨d - 1, by omega⟩
  have hb : b ∈ ((canonicalSymHom A).sectionPieceHom U (e + 1)).range := by
    rw [range_canonicalSymHom_sectionPieceHom_succ A hgen hU]; trivial
  exact hb

/-! ### The closed immersion into `𝐏(𝒜_1)`, and Tag 0B3U -/

variable (hgen : ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A)

/-- **The morphism `Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)` of Stacks Tag 07ZR**, attached to the canonical
graded-algebra map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` and nothing else. -/
def canonicalSymProjHom :
    (relativeProj A).scheme ⟶ (relativeProj (symAlgebra (A.piece 1))).scheme :=
  Tag07ZRVeryAmple.projHom (canonicalSymHom A)
    (relativeMapDomain_eq_top_of_affineSections _
      (eventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections_canonicalSymHom A hgen))

/-- **Stacks Tag 07ZR: the morphism `Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)` is a closed immersion**, for `𝒜`
generated by `𝒜_1` over `𝒜_0`, with no hypothesis on the graded-algebra map because the map is
the canonical one. -/
@[stacks 07ZR "the morphism X -> P(A_1) associated to the canonical map Sym(A_1) -> A is a closed \
immersion"]
theorem isClosedImmersion_canonicalSymProjHom : IsClosedImmersion (canonicalSymProjHom A hgen) :=
  Tag07ZRVeryAmple.isClosedImmersion_projHom_of _ _
    (isClosedImmersion_relativeMapHom_of_affineSections _
      (eventuallySurjectiveOnAffineSections_canonicalSymHom A hgen))

/-- **The closed immersion is a morphism over the base.** -/
theorem canonicalSymProjHom_comp_toBase :
    canonicalSymProjHom A hgen ≫ (relativeProj (symAlgebra (A.piece 1))).toBase =
      (relativeProj A).toBase :=
  Tag07ZRVeryAmple.projHom_comp_toBase (canonicalSymHom A) _

end Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0B3U.** Let `S` be a scheme and `𝒜` a quasi-coherent graded
`𝒪_S`-algebra generated by `𝒜_1` over `𝒜_0` with `𝒜_1` of finite type. Then the projection
`Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ S` is projective.

The source's proof: the canonical graded-algebra map `Sym(𝒜_1) ⟶ 𝒜` induces a closed immersion
`Proj_S(𝒜) ⟶ 𝐏(𝒜_1)` over `S` by Stacks Tag 07ZK (2), and `𝐏(𝒜_1)` is the projective bundle of a
quasi-coherent module of finite type, so that closed immersion is exactly the condition of Stacks
Tag 01W8. -/
@[stacks 0B3U]
theorem isProjective_relativeProj_toBase {S : Scheme.{u}}
    (A : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S)
    (hgen : Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne A)
    (hfin : (A.piece 1).IsFiniteType) :
    IsProjective (relativeProj A).toBase :=
  ⟨A.piece 1, A.isQuasicoherent 1, hfin,
    Stacks.SymGraded.isQuasicoherentPieces_of_isQuasicoherent (A.piece 1),
    Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom A hgen,
    Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.isClosedImmersion_canonicalSymProjHom A hgen,
    Stacks.Tag01VMRelativeVeryAmple.canonicalSymProjHom_comp_toBase A hgen⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
